<title>USA: U.S. may withdraw complaints on EU rice, barley.</title>
<headline>U.S. may withdraw complaints on EU rice, barley.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman's trade adviser Paul Drazek Tuesday said the U.S. may withdraw its request for a dispute panel over European Union rice imports since the EU commission has won the right to decide a new rice import system.</p>
<p>Drazek told reporters after accompanying the secretary to a hearing on Capitol Hill that the department understood the EU may be approving a malting barley regulation tariff rate quota on Tuesday as well.</p>
<p>&quot;If those two things happen and they appear to be acceptable to us, then we probably would withdraw our request for dispute settlement,&quot; Drazek said.</p>
</text>
